                "text": "**Analyzing the Pattern Emerges**\n\nI'm seeing a clear pattern emerging from the first example. The input matrix, a 3x3 square with a bordered 1 and a center 2, is producing an interesting output. The output, when viewed at the same coordinates as the input (r=4..6, c=4..6), doubles the center value.\n\n\n**Investigating the Expansion Process**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the expansion. It seems the output extends outwards in four directions, creating a cross shape. The key is in understanding how the center box changes. Initially, the input's center 1x1 cell gets inverted, while the rest of the center box inverts as well, but also expands outward. The borders use the border color.\n\n\n",
